export interface PreferencesGateway {
  save(value: Preferences): Promise<void>;
  signOut(): Promise<void>;
}

export class PreferencesSession {
  constructor(current: Preferences, gateway: PreferencesGateway);
  get draft(): Preferences;
  replaceCurrent(current: Preferences): void;
  saveDraft(): Promise<void>;
  signOut(): Promise<void>;
}
```

The constructor and `replaceCurrent` must deep-copy their argument. The `draft` getter must return a fresh deep copy, so callers cannot mutate session state through it. `saveDraft` must snapshot the draft when called and queue a gateway `save` operation after all previously requested saves or sign-outs, even if an earlier operation rejected. The gateway must receive a deep copy. `signOut` is queued under the same rule. Calls execute in request order and each returned promise resolves or rejects with its own gateway operation. Empty labels and duplicate labels are valid and their order must be preserved.

